        <article class="tl__row" data-tl-row>
          <figure class="tl__plate"><img src="assets/career-2015.webp" alt="Kimi Antonelli in a kart, 2015" data-ph="plate:1"><span class="tl__scrim"></span><figcaption>first race weekend</figcaption></figure>
          <div class="tl__text">
            <p class="tl__year" data-tl-year>2015</p>
            <h3 class="tl__label">the first kart</h3>
            <p class="tl__note">Eight years old, a rented chassis and a wet Sunday at Lonato. He finished last and asked to go again the same afternoon.</p>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="tl__row" data-tl-row>
          <figure class="tl__plate"><img src="assets/career-2018.webp" alt="Karting championship podium, 2018" data-ph="plate:2"><span class="tl__scrim"></span><figcaption>wsk final round</figcaption></figure>
          <div class="tl__text">
            <p class="tl__year" data-tl-year>2018</p>
            <h3 class="tl__label">national titles</h3>
            <p class="tl__note">Two Italian championships in a single season. The junior programme scouts started turning up at the fence.</p>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="tl__row" data-tl-row>
          <figure class="tl__plate"><img src="assets/career-2021.webp" alt="Formula 4 test, 2021" data-ph="plate:3"><span class="tl__scrim"></span><figcaption>first single-seater test</figcaption></figure>
          <div class="tl__text">
            <p class="tl__year" data-tl-year>2021</p>
            <h3 class="tl__label">into a single-seater</h3>
            <p class="tl__note">Signed to the junior academy in February, in a Formula 4 car by November. Nine hundred kilometres of testing before his first start.</p>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="tl__row" data-tl-row>
          <figure class="tl__plate"><img src="assets/career-2022.webp" alt="Formula 4 champion, 2022" data-ph="plate:4"><span class="tl__scrim"></span><figcaption>double f4 champion</figcaption></figure>
          <div class="tl__text">
            <p class="tl__year" data-tl-year>2022</p>
            <h3 class="tl__label">two championships</h3>
            <p class="tl__note">Italian and German F4 in the same year. Thirteen wins. The first season where the results stopped being a surprise to anyone.</p>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="tl__row" data-tl-row>
          <figure class="tl__plate"><img src="assets/career-2023.webp" alt="Formula Regional, 2023" data-ph="plate:5"><span class="tl__scrim"></span><figcaption>formula regional</figcaption></figure>
          <div class="tl__text">
            <p class="tl__year" data-tl-year>2023</p>
            <h3 class="tl__label">regional, twice over</h3>
            <p class="tl__note">Middle East and European titles back to back. A full winter of simulator work between them, and no off-season to speak of.</p>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="tl__row" data-tl-row>
          <figure class="tl__plate"><img src="assets/career-2024.webp" alt="Formula 2 rookie season, 2024" data-ph="plate:6"><span class="tl__scrim"></span><figcaption>f2 rookie year</figcaption></figure>
          <div class="tl__text">
            <p class="tl__year" data-tl-year>2024</p>
            <h3 class="tl__label">the hard year</h3>
            <p class="tl__note">Straight to Formula 2, skipping a rung. Two wins, four retirements, and the tyre education the step up was really for.</p>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="tl__row" data-tl-row>
          <figure class="tl__plate"><img src="assets/career-2026.webp" alt="Mercedes-AMG F1 debut, 2026" data-ph="plate:7"><span class="tl__scrim"></span><figcaption>race one, melbourne</figcaption></figure>
          <div class="tl__text">
            <p class="tl__year" data-tl-year>2026</p>
            <h3 class="tl__label">driver_012</h3>
            <p class="tl__note">A works seat at eighteen. Points on debut, a podium by round four, and the rest of the grid recalibrating what a rookie is allowed to do.</p>
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>

</div><!-- /stack -->

